                                 Top 1.0
                           Written by Spaceman!

I  had been using MS-TopTen for a while and I liked the output, but wanted
to be able to do different amounts of users...  So I started out writing a
simple  top-users  utility  that  had  a  configurable  number of users to
display...    Once   I   got  that  working,  I  started  working  on  the
configuration...   I kept adding things...  And here is the result...  The
only  other thing on this that I can think of to change is to make all the
text  external  and configurable which will probably be version 2.0...  If
you  can  think  of ANY other suggestions, PLEASE let me know...  Hope you
like it!

                          Configuration format:

3					Number of configurations to follow
2					User account to start at
					Blank line (REQUIRED!!!)
5					How many top users to display
\n1\c9Top Uploaders:\n2			Title
gfiles:Top.005.Uploaders		Filename
\n1\c9Top Downloaders:\n2		Title
gfiles:Top.005.Downloaders		Filename
\n1\c9Top Posters:\n2			Title
gfiles:Top.005.Posters			Filename
\n1\c9Most Credits:\n2			Title
gfiles:Top.005.Credits			Filename
\n1\c9Top Callers:\n2			Title
gfiles:Top.005.Callers			Filename
					Blank line (REQUIRED!!!)
10					How many top users to display
\n1\c9Top Uploaders:\n2			Title
gfiles:Top-Users/Top.010.Uploaders	Filename
\n1\c9Top Downloaders:\n2		Title
gfiles:Top-Users/Top.010.Downloaders	Filename
\n1\c9Top Posters:\n2			Title
gfiles:Top-Users/Top.010.Posters	Filename
\n1\c9Most Credits:\n2			Title
gfiles:Top-Users/Top.010.Credits	Filename
\n1\c9Top Callers:\n2			Title
gfiles:Top-Users/Top.010.Callers	Filename

So you can make plenty of different formats...  Just make sure you get all
the  lines  in  there, including the blanks between each config...  If you
don't  want  to  save  any  file,  just  make  the filename start with a *
character...

                                Versions:

1.0 - Original version...
1.1 - It  used  to be that if you wanted it to create a sorted list of all
      your  users,  you could set it to something like 1000 top users, but
      this  was  slow...   That's  because even when it had read in only 5
      users total, it was sorting all 1000 slots...  It now only sorts the
      filled slots...

